    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0229" n="169" xml:id="pg169"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic">October 31,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1185.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I confirm on the overleaf my telegram of
                    yesterday’s date in regard to the return of the Szechuan commission.</p>
                <p>On leaving Chengtu the commission should go to Chungking, and thence down the
                    Yangtze to Shanghai, using all diligence on the way. From Shanghai Mr. Read and
                    Mr. Cheshire can go to Chefoo by steamer, and from that place overland to
                    Tientsin, if navigation is still closed at that time.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
